{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I deleted the `audit-log-archiver` CronJob and its jobs, then submitted the mitigation. The submission was accepted. I haven't confirmed the cronjob was the cause of the degradation.\n\n- **Why I removed it:** The CronJob was created after the app deployed and ran every minute with `concurrencyPolicy: Allow`. Its `fluent-bit-sidecar` container never exits. So each run left a pod stuck at `1/2 NotReady`, and the pods kept piling up in the namespace.\n- **What I saw before the fix:** All application pods were Running. Requests to the frontend returned 200 with normal latency. The one exception was a slow first request at about 2.5 seconds. I tested hotel search, recommendations, login and reservation.\n- **After the fix:** No stuck pods remain in the namespace. I didn't re-run the request checks after deleting the CronJob.\n- **Other things I saw:** `geo`, `rate`, `reservation` and `user` each restarted once shortly after starting. I didn't look into why, and they have been stable since."}}
